> login to the Github
> Create a new public repository "Chickens"
> Create a new folder in local by using terminal
> Perform "git init"
> Create a new file "touch chickens.txt"
> Add and commit the file " git commit -am "Test"
> Rename master to main "git branch -M main"
> Push the code "git remote add origin url"
> Then perform "git push -u origin main"
> Go to the Github
> Go to the "Settings"
> Scroll down and go to the "Github Pages" section
> Go to local and create a new branch "git switch -c ght-pages"
> Create a html file "touch index.html"
> Add the website contains on the "index.html"
> Then perform commit "git commit -am "Testing"
> Push the code "git push origin ph-pages"
> Go to the Github
> Go to the "Settings"
> Scroll down and go to the "Github Pages" section
> In the source select "gh-pages" branch and "/ (root)" option from dropdown
> Github display a message "Your site is ready to published at https://example.github.io/chickens"
